title: Labor Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
view-if: labor_policy_timer <= 0 and dem_president = 1
on-arrival: labor_policy_timer = 8

= Labor Policy

Unions are the backbone of the party but face headwinds. What can we do for workers?

- @pro_act: Strengthen the right to organize
- @minimum_wage: Raise the minimum wage
- @worker_training: Invest in apprenticeships
- @easy_discard

@pro_act
on-arrival: labor_strength += 5; labor_relation += 8; working_dem += 3*(1-dissent); biz_relation -= 5; labor_dissent -= 6; month_actions += 1

New rules make organizing easier. Business groups mobilize against us.

@minimum_wage
on-arrival: labor_relation += 4; working_dem += 3*(1-dissent); young_dem += 2*(1-dissent); biz_relation -= 3; unemployed += 0.05; month_actions += 1

Millions get raises.

@worker_training
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 budget.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; unemployed -= 0.2; working_dem += 2*(1-dissent); rural_dem += 1*(1-dissent); moderate_strength += 1; month_actions += 1

A skills agenda wins support across lines.
